# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo is PUBLIC — never commit credentials. Covers .env and name.env.
.env
*.env

# ── Auto-fetched DDB party sheets (other players' data) ───────
# ddb_party_sync.js pulls full character sheets players shared only
# "Campaign Only" on D&D Beyond — republishing them to this PUBLIC repo
# would override that choice. Ignore the generated raw JSON + markdown.
# (The hand-written "<Name> - Character Sheet.md" files are NOT affected.)
03-Characters/01 PCs/Party Character Sheets/_raw/
03-Characters/01 PCs/Party Character Sheets/*(DDB).md

# SKILLS.md is generated by claude-artifacts/scripts/skill-usage-audit.ps1 and is
# deliberately NOT published from this repo, which is public. The file may exist
# locally; the cross-project record lives in the private septentrion vault at
# Skills/.system/SKILL-DISTRIBUTION.md. Ignored here so Obsidian Git cannot
# auto-commit it (that is exactly how it reached sitl_vault's public remote on
# 2026-09-27 before the publish decision was made).
SKILLS.md

# Screenshots of admin dashboards. This repo is PUBLIC, and a console capture can
# leak account IDs, game IDs, hostnames and config layout — on 2026-09-29 a
# Cloudflare capture in another vault had the account ID in the FILENAME alone, so
# checking the pixels is not enough. The privacy screen only reads
# .md/.json/.txt/.canvas/.base/.html, so images are invisible to it and Obsidian
# Git would auto-commit them on its timer. Media folders are tracked on purpose,
# so this is by filename pattern. Added 2026-10-01 under the archive note's
# privacy/security exception; nothing matching was tracked at the time.
screencapture-*
**/screencapture-*
*dash.cloudflare*
